course: dictionary
lesson: 10729
title: Standing up for what is right
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uphold is a doing word, so look at what happens around it. When you uphold something, you support it and make sure it is kept. «Defend the weak and the fatherless; uphold the cause of the poor and the oppressed» tells you to stand up for people who are treated unfairly. The word defend sits right beside uphold, and it is a clue that the meaning is close to protect.
explain: Uphold can also be a job. A referee upholds the rules by making sure everyone follows them. A judge upholds a decision when they say the earlier decision was right and keep it. Try the swap check: put "support and keep" in place of uphold. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: You can also uphold a value, such as honesty or respect. This means you defend it and live by it, even when it is hard. Think of a person who always tells the truth, even when a lie would be easier. They are upholding honesty.
fact: Uphold means to support a rule, law or value and make sure it is kept.
fact: A court upholds a decision when it says the earlier decision was correct and keeps it.
fact: Uphold is a verb, and its forms are upholds, upheld and upholding.
fact: «Uphold the cause of the poor and the oppressed» means stand up for people who are treated unfairly.
fact: To uphold a value means to defend it and live by it, like honesty or respect.
exercise: «Defend the weak and the fatherless; uphold the cause of the poor and the oppressed.» What does uphold mean here? | *Support and keep safe | Hide from | Shout loudly at | Drop and forget
exercise: A referee upholds the rules. What does this mean? | The referee changes the rules every game | The referee leaves the game | The referee breaks the rules | *The referee makes sure the rules are kept
exercise: Which word in «Defend the weak and the fatherless; uphold the cause of the poor» means about the same as uphold? | poor | *Defend | weak | fatherless
test: A judge upholds a decision when they say it was correct. What does upholds mean? | Forgets it | Cancels it | Makes a new law | *Keeps it as correct
test: What does it mean to uphold a value? | To lose honesty | *To defend honesty and live by it | To ignore honesty for a day | To make honesty into a game
exam: Which sentence uses uphold correctly? | The police uphold the lunch, eating it quickly | The police uphold the football, kicking it away | The police uphold the rain, stopping it | *The police uphold the law, making sure it is kept
